# THE CORPUS LIVES IN THE PRIVATE wheel-cargo REPO (W-10, 2026-07-26).
# data/ here is a LOCAL working copy — a checkout of mmdm-it/wheel-cargo —
# never tracked in this public engine repo (it held third-party copyrighted
# scripture). Local files stay on disk; git just ignores them. Tests run
# against test/fixtures/ (public-domain); the app fetches data at runtime;
# the deploy ships data via sync-data-to-server.sh from the cargo checkout.
data/

# derived at build time by scripts/precompress-json.mjs (belt — data/ already
# covers these, kept for clarity)
*.json.gz
.snapshot-version

# Session-local licensing working papers (Wilbur's dossiers). The repo is
# public and these are negotiation drafts — they must NEVER be committed.
*.local.md

# SIDEBARS — temporary single-topic discussion threads between Howell, Wilbur
# and Orville (first instance: WORKFLOW-DISCUSSION_20260806.md). Howell's
# ruling 2026-08-06: a sidebar is never committed. Deliberation happens here;
# only the CONCLUSION goes to a blueprint or the ledger, and the sidebar is
# then deleted or archived outside the repo.
#
# Ignored rather than merely agreed, because a sidebar lives untracked in a
# tree where `git add -A` is routine — one careless commit and a document that
# is supposed to be deletable is in a public repository permanently.
*-DISCUSSION_*.md

# Session-local settings — holds the GH_TOKEN (R2). The repo is PUBLIC;
# a token in a committed file is published. Never track this file.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/canary/
